OME HUD Chat Panel - Implementation Spec
Overview
Implement an expanding chat interface within the existing OME HUD overlay. The chat panel should grow dynamically as the user types, reposition intelligently when space runs out, and maintain a scrollable history.

Component Structure
┌─────────────────────────────────────────┐
│  CHAT HISTORY CONTAINER (scrollable)    │
│  ┌───────────────────────────────────┐  │
│  │ [AI Response]                     │  │  ← left-aligned, no indent
│  ├───────────────────────────────────┤  │
│  │   [User Prompt]                   │  │  ← left-aligned, 16-24px indent
│  ├───────────────────────────────────┤  │
│  │ [AI Response]                     │  │
│  └───────────────────────────────────┘  │
├─────────────────────────────────────────┤
│  INPUT TEXTAREA (auto-expanding)        │
│  [grows vertically as user types]       │
└─────────────────────────────────────────┘
        ↑
   Existing HUD controls below (HUD, PROMPT, +/Z/-, atom icon)

Layout & Alignment Rules
Message Alignment (NOT like ChatGPT)

Do NOT use right-align for user messages
Both user and AI messages are LEFT-aligned
Differentiate visually instead:

css.message--user {
  margin-left: 16px;           /* slight indent */
  padding-left: 12px;
  border-left: 2px solid #4a9;  /* subtle accent border */
  background: rgba(255,255,255,0.03);  /* very subtle bg tint */
}

.message--ai {
  margin-left: 0;
  padding-left: 12px;
  border-left: none;
  background: transparent;
}
This keeps the "command/terminal" aesthetic rather than "iMessage conversation" feel.

Expanding Input Behavior
Textarea Auto-Growth
javascript// Textarea should grow as user types (like Slack/Discord)
const textarea = document.querySelector('.hud-chat-input');

textarea.addEventListener('input', () => {
  textarea.style.height = 'auto';  // reset first
  textarea.style.height = textarea.scrollHeight + 'px';
});
Constraints

min-height: 40px (single line)
max-height: 200px (then scroll internally)
When textarea grows, the entire chat panel grows upward


Positioning Logic (The Key Behavior)
Default State

Chat panel sits ABOVE the existing HUD control cluster
Anchored to bottom of viewport (or wherever HUD currently sits)
Panel grows UPWARD as content is added

Collision Detection & Reposition
When the chat panel's top edge hits the viewport top:
javascriptfunction checkAndRepositionHUD() {
  const chatPanel = document.querySelector('.hud-chat-panel');
  const hudContainer = document.querySelector('.hud-container'); // parent of everything
  const rect = chatPanel.getBoundingClientRect();

  // If top of chat panel hits or exceeds viewport top
  if (rect.top <= 0) {
    // Drop the ENTIRE HUD (chat + controls) as a unit
    // Position it 10px from viewport bottom
    hudContainer.style.position = 'fixed';
    hudContainer.style.bottom = '10px';
    hudContainer.style.top = 'auto';

    // Enable scrolling on chat history
    chatPanel.classList.add('scrollable');
  }
}

// Run on:
// - New message added
// - Textarea expansion
// - Window resize
Scrollable State
Once repositioned to bottom:
css.hud-chat-panel.scrollable .chat-history {
  max-height: calc(100vh - 150px);  /* leave room for input + controls */
  overflow-y: auto;
  scroll-behavior: smooth;
}

State Diagram
[INITIAL STATE]
    │
    │  User types / messages added
    │  Panel grows upward
    ▼
[GROWING UPWARD]
    │
    │  Panel top hits viewport top (rect.top <= 0)
    ▼
[REPOSITIONED STATE]
    - Entire HUD drops to bottom: 10px
    - Chat history becomes scrollable
    - New messages scroll into view
    │
    │  User clears/minimizes chat?
    ▼
[RESET TO INITIAL] (optional)

CSS Structure
css.hud-container {
  position: fixed;
  right: 20px;
  bottom: 80px;  /* above your existing control cluster */
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  align-items: flex-end;
  z-index: 9999;
}

.hud-chat-panel {
  width: 400px;  /* or whatever fits your design */
  background: rgba(30, 30, 30, 0.95);
  border-radius: 12px;
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  max-height: calc(100vh - 100px);
}

.chat-history {
  flex: 1;
  padding: 12px;
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  gap: 8px;
  /* scrolling enabled when .scrollable class added */
}

.chat-input-wrapper {
  padding: 8px 12px;
  border-top: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.1);
}

.hud-chat-input {
  width: 100%;
  min-height: 40px;
  max-height: 200px;
  resize: none;
  background: rgba(0,0,0,0.3);
  border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.1);
  border-radius: 8px;
  color: white;
  padding: 10px;
  font-family: inherit;
}

Key Implementation Notes

Grow upward, not downward - Use flex-direction: column with the input at bottom, history above
Check position on every change - Hook checkAndRepositionHUD() into:

Message send/receive
Textarea input event
Window resize


Smooth transitions - Add transition: bottom 0.2s ease for the reposition
Scroll to bottom on new message - When in scrollable state:

javascript   chatHistory.scrollTop = chatHistory.scrollHeight;

Keep existing HUD controls - This chat panel sits ABOVE your existing control cluster (HUD button, PROMPT, +/Z/-, atom) - don't replace them

